# Google Sign-In / Drive backup (optional)
#
# Create an OAuth client in Google Cloud Console:
#   1. Enable the "Google Drive API".
#   2. OAuth consent screen -> External -> add your Gmail as a test user.
#   3. Create an OAuth client of type "Web application" and paste its id below.
#      The Capacitor plugin uses a *web* client id on every platform.
#      On that Web client, add each origin you open (http://localhost:3000 and
#      the deployed site, e.g. https://your-app.vercel.app) to BOTH
#      "Authorized JavaScript origins" and "Authorized redirect URIs".
#      Origin only: https, no path, no trailing slash. That string is the
#      redirect_uri (window.location.origin). Copy it from the Google error
#      page's "error details", not from the accounts.google.com address bar.
#      A trailing slash is a different URI. A preview URL is a different origin.
#   4. Also create an OAuth client of type "Android" with the package name
#      com.dayflow.dailytasks and the SHA-1 of your signing keystore.
#
# The only scope requested is https://www.googleapis.com/auth/drive.appdata,
# which Google classifies as non-sensitive: the app can read and write only its
# own hidden folder inside your Drive.
#
# Leave this empty to build the app without cloud backup (everything else works).
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=""
